<title>SWEDEN: S&amp;P says no plans to upgrade Sweden's ratings.</title>
<headline>S&amp;P says no plans to upgrade Sweden's ratings.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. credit rating agency Standard &amp; Poor's said on Tuesday it had no plans to upgrade Sweden's rating, which is currently AA+ for long-term debt denominated in foreign currency, with a negative outlook.  </p>
<p>S&amp;P Sweden's managing director Marianne Flink dismissed market speculation the credit rating agency was about to upgrade Sweden's ratings.</p>
<p>&quot;I have heard there are rumours but this time, it really is ridiculous as we have, as late as August, just confirmed Sweden's ratings,&quot; Flink told Reuters.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1045</p>
</text>
